# Which layer is composed from which, without the conversion factors. One row per part: the
# composed layer, the part it is composed from, and whether the part is local to the composing
# document.
#
# Which layer, never how much, and leaving it out is the point
#   examples/diagramming composes this and nothing wider, so the emitter cannot read a figure at
#   all. Which layer feeds which can be drawn and the figures cannot, and a diagram carries the
#   first. An emitter that could see a figure could render one, and a figure drawn in a notation
#   with no unit is the meaningless product entries/cross_layer_edges.sqlc names
#   `the_product_nobody_should_use`.
#
# A type error, not a design decision
#   Reading the wider relation does not compile: sqlx has no mapping for `pm.absence_reason`, and
#   needs a feature for NUMERIC. The schema refuses to hand a figure to a program with no use for
#   one, which is the DDL's typed blanks paying off in a second language.
-- composition/parts.sqlc reduced to which layer is composed from which; one call activity per part.
SELECT p.composition, p.composed_layer, p.part_notation, p.part_filing, p.part_layer,
       (p.part_filing = p.composition) AS is_local
FROM (
    :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
) p
